WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.340
Mappy Land!

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:06.240
Mappy has dynamic plans for himself and his girlfriend, Mappico.

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:30.480
That's neat. And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:32.580
I'm Mike. I'm Sean.

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:33.900
I'm Joe.

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:35.160
And I'm Sam.

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:41.840
That is some important deep lore information for people that don't know that Mappy Land is

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:44.800
just the land and Mappy is the character.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:46.640
And he also has a girlfriend named Mappico.

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:53.400
And then you follow him through the big life events of Mappy.

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:58.020
He does adult things.

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:00.080
This is sounding like Smurfs.

00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:02.520
I got a Smurfs vibe from it too.

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:06.340
It really is though at the end of the day, it's the ultimate cat and mouse game.

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:08.240
Am I right? Oh, wow.

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:09.140
Oh, shit.

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:12.120
I didn't really see it that way.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:18.980
I mean, it's not cat and mouse like someone chasing someone, but it is literally a cat

00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:23.420
and mouse game. You could argue though that the cats are chasing Mappy.

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:24.660
They're chasing him. That's true.

00:01:26.780 --> 00:01:28.840
I thought this was more like Catch Me If You Can.

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:30.180
Which it very well could be.

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:31.020
Leonardo DiCaprio movie.

00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:32.900
Yeah. Leonardo DiCaprio movie.

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:34.400
Yeah. It very well could be though.

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:35.640
We don't know what Mappy.

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:37.940
We don't know he's innocent. We only get to see him.

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:39.280
We just start playing as him.

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:40.400
We don't know what he did.

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:42.740
He could have had a life of crime before this game started.

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:44.720
I choose to believe that.

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:48.080
I thought this was like a prequel to MapQuest.

00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:52.500
Yeah, this is how people got around.

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:54.220
They would put this in their car instead of the GPS.

00:01:54.740 --> 00:02:00.240
Yeah. It's a sequel though to a game called Mappy for the arcades.

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:03.140
So they added it instead of it just being about the mouse itself.

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:06.360
Now it's about like the land that he lives in.

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:08.220
So that was a pretty cool upgrade.

00:02:09.220 --> 00:02:12.320
Now, are you are you being funny or is it actually a sequel?

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:15.860
I always assumed that Mappy was just another name for the same game.

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:17.500
Nope. It's the sequel.

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:19.080
This is Mappy.

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:24.640
Mappy was an arcade game and Mappy is kind of like a Bandai Namco mascot in some ways.

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:30.980
I think about like if Q-Bert is a B tier arcade mascot, what tier is Mappy?

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:33.640
It's gotta be like F.

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:35.060
F tier mascot.

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:42.940
Cool. Unless you want to give him a D because you know you want to be nice to him.

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:47.100
I don't know. Yeah, like as far as like recognizability, I'd probably go F.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:51.240
And to be clear when I said I always thought that Mappy was etc, etc.

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:55.260
I mean always as in like since yesterday when I heard about this for the first time.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:03:02.420
I would say at least D because he has Smash Brothers representation, right?

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:04.980
That's true. Everybody has Smash Brothers representation.

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:06.580
Yeah, but he has a...

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:15.300
Everybody's here. I'm sure. Am I correct in saying that Pac-Man's up B is based on the trampolines in this game?

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:16.800
Absolutely. Yeah, alright.

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:18.700
Is that correct? No way. Really?

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:20.140
I'm being dead serious.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.460
It's absolutely true.

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:27.380
As you guys know from playing the game, the trampolines that Mappy jumps on both in the

00:03:27.380 --> 00:03:32.240
original arcade game and in Mappy Land for the NES, you can only bounce on them three times

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:33.860
and then they disappear.

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:39.940
Here, the very same thing happens to Pac-Man in Super Smash Brothers where he can get three

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:43.460
up Bs, each one higher than the one before it, but then it's gone.

00:03:43.960 --> 00:03:44.820
It's crazy.

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:46.900
I never made that connection while I was playing.

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:52.900
Alright, so let's actually talk about the game though, because I think that there is something,

00:03:53.140 --> 00:03:57.240
there is an interesting element here because it's, on the surface, it's just an arcade platformer,

00:03:57.300 --> 00:04:02.000
right? It's no different than a lot of other games that we've played like City Connection or,

00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:08.540
you know, I'll even liken it to Pac-Man because the ultimate goal is just like a set stage where

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:12.080
you just have to collect certain, I think they're cheeses, right?

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:14.920
You have to collect the cheese and once you've collected all the...

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:16.780
If in one of them it's cheese.

00:04:17.300 --> 00:04:19.560
Yeah, well no, because then there's like keys eventually, right?

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:21.040
That sounds like cheese.

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:27.600
Cheese, keys, rings, Christmas trees, lots of E's.

00:04:28.020 --> 00:04:32.280
Right, so you have to collect those things and then you're like good to pass on to the stage.

00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:40.300
The thing that makes Mappy different from the other platformers is the trampoline element of the game

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:46.160
and, you know, otherwise like the cats are pretty much just like the ghosts in Pac-Man.

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:51.520
They just have like this random thing that some of them are coherent, other ones just go wherever they want.

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:57.280
The, you know, the actual structures are always on the same types of platforms.

00:04:57.460 --> 00:05:01.260
There's only ever like three types of platform levels that you can be on.

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:05.640
So the layouts themselves don't change that much and the style of the game doesn't change that much.

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:12.120
But how your access to these trampolines and where the prizes are placed changes between rounds.

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:17.100
And that's really like the key defining element of each land besides the setting.

00:05:17.320 --> 00:05:19.000
Sean, anything you want to add to that?

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:21.740
No, that's pretty much it.

00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:27.460
Like the only, the only thing that happens as you progress, I think, is the arrangement.

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:30.480
The arrangement and the window dressing.

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:36.580
It doesn't really add any, any other gameplay elements as you move forward.

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:40.180
It just recolors everything pretty much.

00:05:40.720 --> 00:05:43.500
I feel a little differently, actually.

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:51.860
I felt like, my first thought was, you know, this, whenever we get a game like this that's arcadey, it always kind of throws me off a little bit.

00:05:51.940 --> 00:05:57.100
Because it feels, this like arcade style game feels like something we were seeing in 1985, 1986.

00:05:57.440 --> 00:05:59.500
So it's always strange to be like for one to pop up again.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:06.160
But I did think that these, it had some unique ways of going about gameplay.

00:06:06.340 --> 00:06:12.500
And I actually thought that there were some interesting, each level had some different, I mean, there's a level later on where you would just fly.

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:14.480
The whole, you fly and you shoot enemies.

00:06:14.760 --> 00:06:16.480
Totally different than the rest of the game.

00:06:16.740 --> 00:06:20.200
And then there's like a level where there's, where there's a cannon that you can shoot at people.

00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:24.940
And there's always different, different ways of dispatching the enemies.

00:06:25.020 --> 00:06:29.360
I thought that there was actually like, I was surprised that there was some variety as I went on.

00:06:30.740 --> 00:06:32.160
Yeah, there's different traps.

00:06:32.420 --> 00:06:34.540
Yeah. I apologize for that.

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:42.460
And there's also one level with vines too, where you're jumping from vine to vine and the platforms are, the trampolines are moving.

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:45.300
So it, it does change it up a little bit.

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:47.800
Yeah. The vines were the awakening for me.

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:57.140
That's when I realized like that this game was a step up from Mappy, the original, because they were actually taking the idea of integrating the settings.

00:06:57.140 --> 00:07:00.420
You know, Sam, you just mentioned the vines.

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:03.500
And I thought that was really unique and reminded me of Donkey Kong Jr.

00:07:03.780 --> 00:07:06.380
in a lot of ways in the way that he would climb the vines.

00:07:06.380 --> 00:07:14.500
But then, you know, to Joe's point, when you get on the balloon power up and now you can fly and that's the level where you're collecting the keys and taking down the ghosts.

00:07:15.040 --> 00:07:32.080
I think it's surprising that the game doesn't just stick to trampolines that, you know, that access you to platforms because the, correct me if I'm wrong, guys, but like the trampoline layout as it by itself, like the first like couple levels of the game are very, very simple.

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:37.860
Right. Like, did anybody ever fall into the trap of like having to use the trampoline three times and then falling in the pit?

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:46.560
I feel like there's enough leeway between where they place the enemies and how the enemies behave that you can mostly fool them on like the first jump of your trampoline.

00:07:46.660 --> 00:07:49.100
You should never really run out of trampoline jumps.

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:53.400
I actually didn't even know that you could run out of trampoline jumps.

00:07:54.540 --> 00:08:00.100
Yeah, especially since you're invincible, you're invincible when you're using the trampoline.

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:03.980
It's really hard to to die there.

00:08:04.680 --> 00:08:20.040
The game more or less is like not just the trampolines, but I found most of it to be very simplistic, including these these vines you can hang off of, including the flying,

00:08:20.040 --> 00:08:26.080
the one flying screen or four flying screens, depending on how much you're playing.

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:30.180
So, yeah, very simple design overall.

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:44.260
All right. Let's talk about the weapons in the game, because that's another thing that's that's pretty unique to Mappy Land is there are optional power ups or weapons that you can collect in the stages.

00:08:44.260 --> 00:08:49.820
And I believe they transfer over between levels so you don't have to use them.

00:08:49.960 --> 00:08:51.520
Yeah, you don't have to use them right away.

00:08:52.520 --> 00:08:57.560
And, you know, to Joe's point earlier, there's some that are like built into the stages that are pretty cool.

00:08:57.940 --> 00:09:04.680
I think there's like a a bar that you can do like front flips on to stay away from people.

00:09:04.920 --> 00:09:09.220
There's a punching bag that you can like hit and then it'll hit a cat if they're nearby.

00:09:09.580 --> 00:09:12.500
But there's also the ones that you just like drop on the fly, too.

00:09:12.880 --> 00:09:16.900
And I thought there was like a there was like a Tom and Jerry element to that.

00:09:17.060 --> 00:09:20.540
Forget the cat and mouse thing, but just like in a cartoon world, too.

00:09:20.780 --> 00:09:26.360
There's something really funny about the way that Mappy handles his cat enemies.

00:09:27.060 --> 00:09:29.000
I don't know if you guys felt the same way, Joe.

00:09:29.860 --> 00:09:30.780
Yeah, I mean, definitely.

00:09:30.780 --> 00:09:39.080
And just to speak to the first element that you were talking about, you know, the the environmental elements that you use.

00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:45.520
Since those to me felt like the primary thing, at least at the beginning, before you had collected droppables.

00:09:45.680 --> 00:09:47.780
And I thought that that at first I thought was very annoying.

00:09:48.020 --> 00:09:49.860
And then after I thought about it, I was like, it's actually kind of interesting.

00:09:50.020 --> 00:09:57.120
It's a different way to play the game and play a game like this where I'm I have to almost exclusively use my environment to to attack things.

00:09:57.120 --> 00:09:59.500
And there were unique ways to use those environment things.

00:09:59.500 --> 00:10:03.880
And of course, later on, you get you quickly get other droppables.

00:10:03.980 --> 00:10:15.180
But I always felt like those environmental like defense mechanisms were were more present and which I just thought was an interesting unique choice in a game like this.

00:10:15.600 --> 00:10:16.720
Yeah, I enjoyed those.

00:10:16.920 --> 00:10:25.180
I had a fun moment with like I think it was the punching bag or thing, whatever that thing was, where it just knocked away two enemies.

00:10:25.400 --> 00:10:27.400
And I didn't even realize that's what it did.

00:10:28.860 --> 00:10:32.040
And for the most part, I didn't.

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:39.960
I think because I had because you start with nothing when I pressed, what is it, the B button or the A button?

00:10:41.180 --> 00:10:45.860
I forget which one is which it and nothing happens.

00:10:45.860 --> 00:10:52.320
And I just assumed that you didn't use items or you didn't throw things or whatever.

00:10:52.320 --> 00:10:55.320
So for most of my playthrough, I didn't use anything.

00:10:56.320 --> 00:10:58.380
And it I think it was fine.

00:10:58.580 --> 00:11:03.600
It went OK. And then when I realized you could, I was like, oh, that makes it a lot easier.

00:11:04.780 --> 00:11:09.320
So I don't even think that they're really that necessary for for for most levels anyway.

00:11:10.580 --> 00:11:13.020
Yeah, they're like an added color to the game.

00:11:13.160 --> 00:11:17.740
You know, I was I was giving that cartoon analogy, but I kind of wish they even doubled down on it a little more.

00:11:17.900 --> 00:11:25.520
Right. Like what if you did like reverse mousetrap where the objective was actually to trap the cats instead of collecting prizes?

00:11:25.960 --> 00:11:38.840
I thought that, you know, there could have been some more hijinks, you know, in the levels that really play to the to the settings that you're in, too, because Joe mentioned that you can fire off like cannonballs and stuff like that.

00:11:38.860 --> 00:11:50.740
I just thought it would have been fun to do like some some more things that actually involve the enemies in a way that like it makes it a cat and mouse game where they're trying to catch you before you catch them.

00:11:50.940 --> 00:11:52.300
More of like a systems feel.

00:11:53.340 --> 00:11:55.140
Yeah, I think that's fair to say.

00:11:55.140 --> 00:11:58.740
Or even just, you know, like it doesn't have to be a whole different kind of game.

00:11:58.860 --> 00:12:16.500
I mean, maybe what I'm proposing is like a spiritual successor to Mappy Land, but it could also have just been more cartoon like in the sense of, you know, add anvils and pulling pianos like, you know, just double down on that idea because it seems like they went there and they just were like nervous about getting too close to Looney Tunes land.

00:12:17.340 --> 00:12:20.440
Yeah, but they were good at doing with the with the amount that they did.

00:12:20.520 --> 00:12:24.940
I wish they had done more also, but like making it all feel like shenanigans.

00:12:24.940 --> 00:12:35.400
You know, like there's there's there was one like cat toy that if you if you if you fling it as you walk by the cats will just get distracted for a minute and like they look all happy and they like dance around it.

00:12:35.400 --> 00:12:39.520
And like everything had a different effect on the cats and it was all helpful to you.

00:12:39.640 --> 00:12:43.820
And some of the effects were just aesthetic and like did fundamentally the same thing.

00:12:43.820 --> 00:12:47.980
But it just gave it a little bit of like, oh, this feels like yeah, kind of Looney Tunes like you're saying.

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:50.980
Did anybody find out about the bonus level?

00:12:53.980 --> 00:12:55.200
I'm going to take that for a no.

00:12:56.520 --> 00:12:58.160
It's not easy to find.

00:12:58.400 --> 00:13:04.500
And I only saw it in a in a gameplay video I was watching on YouTube and I was like, how would you ever know to do this?

00:13:04.600 --> 00:13:06.000
I guess that was like the point of it.

00:13:06.120 --> 00:13:09.860
You know, a lot of bonus levels are like encouraged for people to stumble upon.

00:13:09.860 --> 00:13:15.400
This is like you take a leap of faith and you either get to the bonus round or not.

00:13:15.560 --> 00:13:20.360
It doesn't again in a game like this that's kind of simple and not that hard to fight off against.

00:13:20.620 --> 00:13:22.260
I don't think the bonus level is that rewarding.

00:13:22.260 --> 00:13:26.160
So it's more for like players who figure it out to score extra points.

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:34.180
But essentially you have to like figure out which trampoline is like the one that you can jump on three times.

00:13:34.660 --> 00:13:46.440
And then instead of it killing Mappy by dropping him into the pitfall, it will shoot him up into the clouds where there are like a bunch of different items and points to collect and stuff like that.

00:13:46.540 --> 00:13:50.080
But I just don't know how you would figure that out without accidentally trying to die.

00:13:50.900 --> 00:13:52.940
Yeah, yeah. We're just too good.

00:13:53.100 --> 00:13:55.020
We're too good to find the bonus level.

00:13:56.160 --> 00:13:56.960
Well, it's not even that.

00:13:57.080 --> 00:13:59.200
Yes, of course, that's what it is for us.

00:13:59.340 --> 00:14:04.420
But for most people even, it's like it's not every single trampoline.

00:14:04.480 --> 00:14:06.340
So you wouldn't know if you found the right one.

00:14:06.560 --> 00:14:09.120
You wouldn't even know if it's in that stage because it's not in all the stages.

00:14:10.660 --> 00:14:13.500
Is it fixed or is it like random?

00:14:14.400 --> 00:14:15.240
Which one is it?

00:14:15.360 --> 00:14:16.680
So it's like players in the know.

00:14:16.940 --> 00:14:20.720
I think it's actually spread out across a lot of the different levels.

00:14:20.800 --> 00:14:24.900
So I don't remember like if it's 1-4 or 1-3 or whatever.

00:14:24.900 --> 00:14:28.840
But, you know, if you go on like game FAQs, you can find all of them.

00:14:28.920 --> 00:14:41.440
But I feel like it's one of those things that like meant a lot to people who were trying to get the high scores in the games because you have to find all of those to get the highest possible score because that stuff gives you a ton more points than you're getting in the base game.

00:14:42.680 --> 00:14:43.540
The base game.

00:14:44.920 --> 00:14:46.600
It's a whole nother world up there, Sean.

00:14:47.220 --> 00:14:48.420
The DLC land.

00:14:51.420 --> 00:14:53.020
We were having this debate at the beginning.

00:14:53.180 --> 00:15:02.760
I think we all agree that the settings are very interesting and it's nice that they, you know, they didn't just be like, okay, you're just in a world of ladders and platforms.

00:15:02.760 --> 00:15:11.560
Like, you know, I think we had that discussion with City Connection where it was like, yeah, it's cool that they're taking you from like New York to Egypt and stuff like that.

00:15:11.660 --> 00:15:12.640
But it was just backgrounds.

00:15:12.860 --> 00:15:15.260
It didn't really matter. Here it feels like it matters a little more.

00:15:15.260 --> 00:15:22.500
But I want to challenge everybody to see if this was the most effective route that they could have done in terms of level design.

00:15:22.660 --> 00:15:29.780
Did it actually, did it change the core game of trampolines and going up ladders all that much?

00:15:29.900 --> 00:15:39.620
Should they have designed some puzzle things where you could accidentally get trapped in a certain situation and then, you know, you have to try to get out before the cat comes down there or something?

00:15:40.260 --> 00:15:41.420
I'm kind of spitballing here.

00:15:41.620 --> 00:15:43.880
So, Joe, you were a big fan of the level layouts.

00:15:43.980 --> 00:15:56.460
What do you think about that? I mean, yeah, I definitely think that like when I say I'm a big fan of the level layouts, I'm talking as to basically maybe what I expected this game to be when I first booted it up compared to like what it turned out to be.

00:15:56.560 --> 00:15:57.380
It surprised me.

00:15:57.440 --> 00:15:59.180
I thought it was going to be a lot simpler than it was.

00:15:59.960 --> 00:16:04.000
But I do, yeah, I do think there could be a little more variety.

00:16:04.020 --> 00:16:12.720
If you're going to do have like a couple of levels that are kind of doing the same thing, almost exactly the same thing with like a couple of different environmental changes.

00:16:12.720 --> 00:16:14.840
And then you just have one level that's like totally different.

00:16:15.060 --> 00:16:16.520
And then you go back to the same thing again.

00:16:16.680 --> 00:16:18.320
And then you maybe have another one that's totally different.

00:16:18.480 --> 00:16:23.460
It just feels like they had like three ideas and it didn't stretch out long.

00:16:24.040 --> 00:16:25.360
I shouldn't say like three ideas.

00:16:25.440 --> 00:16:26.940
There's a lot of interesting ideas in this game.

00:16:26.940 --> 00:16:33.800
But like three major ideas for level design and they needed to stretch it out a lot across what, like seven levels, eight levels.

00:16:33.980 --> 00:16:37.020
So they just like duplicated a bunch of them and like made minor differences.

00:16:37.280 --> 00:16:46.060
So, yeah, I think that like almost in the same breath, I want to commend them for being having such unique variety.

00:16:46.180 --> 00:16:50.920
And then also kind of like complain about like there not being enough variety.

00:16:50.920 --> 00:16:52.260
So maybe I'm just a complainer.

00:16:52.260 --> 00:16:55.480
But that's kind of the way for some reason, that's kind of how I felt about it.

00:16:56.480 --> 00:17:08.240
My problem with the level design here wasn't so much that like the trampolines and the platforms, like that's the constant.

00:17:08.660 --> 00:17:15.340
And then with every new level, like, yeah, the background changes, the trap changes.

00:17:15.340 --> 00:17:22.260
And then there's like one little core thing that changes, like the like the what's it called?

00:17:22.760 --> 00:17:28.140
The vines or the flying in the ghost, the ghost area.

00:17:28.140 --> 00:17:39.700
But my problem is that these levels are so short and these ideas are so basic that they're they're very they're very shallow.

00:17:40.040 --> 00:17:50.680
Like maybe if they were to add as the game went on, like maybe they introduced the vines and then in level four, they still have vines.

00:17:50.800 --> 00:17:52.240
But now they're introducing something else.

00:17:52.240 --> 00:18:02.660
And if they just layered it more and like made them work off of each other instead of like just like here's an idea for three minutes of your time.

00:18:02.840 --> 00:18:09.320
And now here's a new idea that can work in it like in itself, like in some in some games.

00:18:09.460 --> 00:18:14.120
But in this one, they were too skin deep to hold up on their own for me.

00:18:14.280 --> 00:18:26.600
For me. Yeah, that actually makes me realize that I think what what my issue is with the two is is not now that you mentioned that it feels like like the vine level feels like it's the introduction level to the vine world.

00:18:26.800 --> 00:18:29.720
Like, you know, it should be three more levels where they build on that.

00:18:29.840 --> 00:18:31.260
And then we go on to the flying level.

00:18:31.380 --> 00:18:33.400
And it's so simple because it's teaching you.

00:18:33.820 --> 00:18:37.200
And then like before we get to do any more flying stuff, we just move on.

00:18:37.340 --> 00:18:39.660
It feels like there should be like a couple more flying levels now.

00:18:39.860 --> 00:18:42.260
Now here's where the challenging flying stuff comes.

00:18:42.460 --> 00:18:43.960
So it does feel like they're all.

00:18:44.800 --> 00:18:50.020
They're all good ideas, but they don't go further with any of them.

00:18:50.800 --> 00:18:55.620
Exactly. There's also an element to, you know, the the Meowkies.

00:18:55.900 --> 00:18:59.960
I think they're called those cats that that are trying to catch you.

00:19:00.820 --> 00:19:04.680
They're not that challenging to avoid in most scenarios.

00:19:04.680 --> 00:19:10.240
Like, yes, if you're if you're playing and you're just trying to collect the stuff as fast as you can.

00:19:10.240 --> 00:19:14.880
And sure, like you could run into them pretty quickly or, you know, be careless or something.

00:19:14.900 --> 00:19:21.820
But if you're if you're taking the game kind of slow and you're watching where the cats are, it's very easy to avoid them.

00:19:21.960 --> 00:19:24.560
There's very few like traps or or pitfalls.

00:19:24.560 --> 00:19:35.060
A lot of the trampoline element because you're invisible, not invisible, because you can't be hurt when you're on the trampoline, even though it's like you and like three other cats all bouncing on this trampoline.

00:19:35.540 --> 00:19:37.560
You know, for some reason, you can't be hurt.

00:19:38.060 --> 00:19:44.340
You just got to like choose a way out and make sure that they're not like on the same platform as you at the same time.

00:19:44.760 --> 00:19:49.640
And then you're like free to run in another direction while they're still bouncing on the trampoline.

00:19:50.160 --> 00:19:51.220
And it was like.

00:19:52.260 --> 00:19:56.260
That seemed that seemed like a missed opportunity to make the game just a little bit harder.

00:19:57.280 --> 00:20:04.700
If not, not that it's not if you were hurt on the trampoline, but in the sense that like it's too easy to get away from them, provided you're near one.

00:20:05.620 --> 00:20:20.440
Yeah. And also, like, I know you guys were using the level traps a lot, but like at a certain point I had enough fish that I could just spam fish at these things and I wouldn't have to interact with the level traps at all.

00:20:20.440 --> 00:20:29.080
So if I ever got into a situation where if I went one way or the other, I was going to get touched by a Meowkey.

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:32.320
Otherwise, I could just keep hoarding fish.

00:20:46.280 --> 00:20:48.700
I have a question about the ghost level.

00:20:49.360 --> 00:20:53.980
Go for it. I got to the end of it and there was just like a little man there who wouldn't let me go.

00:20:54.240 --> 00:20:55.940
Is there something else I was supposed to do?

00:20:57.480 --> 00:20:59.580
You have to go.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:07.080
You see, you pick up that little cross thing or whatever, and then you have to go to the entrance of like the church.

00:21:07.360 --> 00:21:10.900
Oh. And then there's a regular like chutes and ladders level.

00:21:11.500 --> 00:21:12.960
Really? Yeah.

00:21:13.420 --> 00:21:17.620
Oh. Maybe just because like I'm Jewish, I just like avoided the church.

00:21:17.800 --> 00:21:22.400
I don't know. I don't even realize there.

00:21:22.800 --> 00:21:23.620
Did I even see a church?

00:21:23.620 --> 00:21:25.700
Well, it was a different objective though, right?

00:21:25.920 --> 00:21:34.800
You are bringing up a good point, Sam, that they don't spell that out for you because the whole time you're collecting cheeses before that, and then all of a sudden there's an icon for keys.

00:21:35.560 --> 00:21:36.720
Yeah, keys. I'm sorry.

00:21:36.820 --> 00:21:39.780
Not that true. Yeah, but even if you collect all of them.

00:21:40.100 --> 00:21:40.960
Yeah, I got all of them.

00:21:41.040 --> 00:21:41.860
All of the keys. No, I know what I'm saying.

00:21:41.920 --> 00:21:46.560
Even if you collect them all, going back to the guy doesn't solve the problem.

00:21:47.000 --> 00:21:53.140
Yeah. Yeah, I totally stumbled into that too because I was just trying to figure out where to go, see if I missed something.

00:21:53.280 --> 00:21:56.020
